# File spec for ./lint.rs. The dispatcher and the exit-1 trap belong to ./mod.sdd.
# Every lint RULE outside this file lives under ./../linting/ whose specs are pending —
# it is named as collaborator here, never restated.

Spec: PackageLint

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  The `agent package lint` leaf — the static, offline package linter driver: parse the CLI
    flags, gate `package.yaml` (missing/parse/unfilled-field cases short-circuit), apply the
    structure and manifest rules this file owns (unexpected directory, required fields,
    OpenAPI option schemas, pre-release versions with text-scanned line attribution), then
    orchestrate the delegated Handlebars and Rhai checkers over the whole package tree and
    the two inline script sites, print the report in `text` or `json` through the shared
    collector, optionally write a JUnit XML artifact, and turn "any Error-level finding"
    into one @Err (@common::Error::YamlError) that ./mod.sdd traps as exit 1.

References:
  ./mod.sdd — caller and exit lane: any @Err from @run is Display-logged
    `Linting the package failed with: {e:}` via @tracing::error! then @std::process::exit(1);
    @Ok falls off the dispatcher and exits 0; this file neither logs nor exits.
  ./../linting/mod.rs, ./../linting/config.rs, ./../linting/hbs_checker.rs,
    ./../linting/rhai_checker.rs — every one spec pending: the @LintResultCollector /
    @LintFinding / @LintLevel model, @LintConfig::load + rule-level resolution and inline
    disables, and all `hbs/…` and `rhai/…` rules; named here only as call-site contract,
    their behaviour is owned there.
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @read_package_yaml, @VynilPackageSource, @VynilPackageType,
    @VynilPackageRequirement::Prefly and the @Schema (openapiv3) re-export the option check
    round-trips against.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — @common::Error / @common::Result contract; every raise here is
    @Error::YamlError.
  ./test.sdd — sibling leaf defining the twin @OutputFormat (duplication `[?]` is tracked
    there).
  /common/src/tools.sdd — approved calibration reference for style and detail.
  /docs/cli.md, /docs/tooling/lint.md — user docs for this subcommand; both diverge from the
    code today (see Tasks).

Depends on:
  ./../linting/: @LintResultCollector (@new/@add/@extend/@has_errors/@prefix_files/@to_text/
    @to_json/@to_junit), @LintFinding, @LintLevel (@Info/@Warn/@Error, @Ord = display rank),
    @LintConfig::load, @find_option_line_numbers, @hbs_checker::HbsChecker,
    @rhai_checker::RhaiChecker — pending specs.
  @common::vynilpackage::read_package_yaml and the source model — manifest load.
  @clap (@Args, @ValueEnum), @serde_json (option round-trip), @std::fs — direct.
  JUnit XML generation is not here: it lives in @LintResultCollector::to_junit (pending).

Exposes:
  @Parameters — `#[derive(@clap::Args, @Debug)]`, all fields @pub (unlike ./test.sdd's); six
    args frozen verbatim: `-p`/`--package-dir`/env `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY` default `/tmp/package`
    (@package_dir); `-c`/`--config-dir`/env `CONFIG_DIR` default `.` (@config_dir, help text
    `Configuration directory` but it only feeds the Rhai import resolver — see Tasks);
    `-s`/`--script-dir`/env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY` with matching value name, default
    `./agent/scripts`, @Option<@std::path::PathBuf> @script_dir — declared @Option yet clap
    fills the default, so it never reaches @None after a parse; `--format` with
    `default_value = "text"` and no env; `--level` with `default_value = "all"` and no env;
    `--junit-output-filename`/env `JUNIT_OUTPUT_FILENAME` optional, its doc help text is
    `` `JUnit` output file `` — the literal ASCII backticks around JUnit are part of the
    help string in source. Env binds only when the flag is absent; flag over env over
    default.
  @OutputFormat — @pub @clap::ValueEnum @Text/`text`, @Json/`json` (`#[value(name = …)]`,
    @Clone/@Debug, no @Default — the arg default string arms it); duplicated by ./test.rs's
    identical enum (pending `[?]` there).
  @LevelFilter — @pub @clap::ValueEnum @All/`all`, @Warn/`warn`, @Error/`error`; display
    floor only, @level_filter_to_lint_level maps All→@LintLevel::Info, Warn→@Warn,
    Error→@Error.
  @run — `pub fn @run(args: &@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>`; synchronous, called by
    ./mod.sdd's exit-1 arm.
  All four exist only within the crate: `mod lint;` in ./mod.rs is private.
  File-private machinery (not surface, frozen below): @expected_dirs, @check_unexpected_dirs,
    @check_manifest_fields, @check_options, @check_prerelease_versions, @is_prerelease,
    @find_line_with_key, @find_image_tag_line, @run_hbs_checks, @run_rhai_checks,
    @scan_hbs_files, @scan_rhai_files, @scan_rhai_files_for_values, @format_output,
    @level_filter_to_lint_level.

Accepts:
  A clap-parsed @Parameters by reference; no path existence check before the manifest gate —
    a bogus or missing @package_dir simply fails the gate below.
  A package directory whose `package.yaml` deserializes as @VynilPackageSource per
    /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd (unknown and extra files are fine, absent sections fine).
  An optional `<package_dir>/.vynil-lint.yaml` consumed by @LintConfig::load (pending); a
    missing/invalid file falls back to defaults there, never an error here.

Returns:
  @Ok(()) iff zero findings carry @LintLevel::Error after the full pipeline — Warn/Info-only
    runs and fully clean runs both land here, and the dispatcher exits 0.
  @Err @common::Error::YamlError in exactly four lanes (Raises); ./mod.sdd turns each into
    the exit-1 line.

Raises:
  @Error::YamlError("Missing package manifest") — `package.yaml` absent at @package_dir
    (the path `exists()` gate, so an existing-but-unreadable file takes the parse lane
    instead); the `package/missing-manifest` @Error finding is printed before this @Err.
  @Error::YamlError("Invalid package manifest") — @read_package_yaml failed for any reason
    (I/O or serde — the distinction survives only inside the printed
    `Failed to parse package.yaml: {e}` finding text).
  @Error::YamlError("Failed to write JUnit output: {e}") — @std::fs::write of the JUnit file
    (missing parent dir first among them), via @map_err.
  @Error::YamlError("Linting failed with errors") — @LintResultCollector::has_errors after
    output and junit lanes; the failing findings themselves are in the printed report only.
  The three non-parse lanes misuse the @YamlError variant for non-YAML failures (Tasks).
  No panic site exists inside this file: zero @unwrap/@expect/@panic! and no indexing (see
    Must posture); the JUnit lane crosses into @to_junit, documented pending-side to
    @panic! only on in-memory-serialization impossibilities.

Handles:
  @package_dir missing entirely — indistinguishable from an empty one: same
    `package/missing-manifest` short-circuit.
  Manifest parses but fields are present-yet-empty (serde requires the keys, so only
    `name: ""`-style values reach this) — one `Missing required field: {field}` @Error per
    field, checks continue.
  Options section absent — @check_options returns after the (already-executed)
    @find_option_line_numbers file read; no findings.
  Option line key missing from the @find_option_line_numbers scan — @None line, finding
    stands without a line number.
  Directory walks that fail at OS level (@read_dir unreadable, non-UTF-8 file read) —
    silently skipped by @if-@Ok/@let-@Ok guards; the scan fns therefore always return
    @Ok(@()) and the `?` propagation in @run_hbs_checks/@run_rhai_checks is dead in practice
    (Tasks `[?]`).
  @metadata.usage — @VynilPackageType drives @expected_dirs; the serde default `tenant` type
    is reached whenever `type:` is omitted upstream.

Must:
  # Pipeline order (frozen exactly; each step feeds the one collector)
  Gate 1: `package.yaml` must @Path::exists at @package_dir; absent → add the
    `package/missing-manifest` Error finding, @prefix_files, @println! the filtered report,
    and return the missing-manifest @Err — no other checker runs and the junit lane is never
    reached on this path.
  Gate 2: @read_package_yaml @Err → add `package/invalid-manifest` Error with the @serde_yaml
    detail interpolated into the message, @prefix_files, @println! the report, return the
    invalid-manifest @Err — same full short-circuit.
  Then in order: @check_manifest_fields (empty-field scan for `name`, `category`,
    `description`, `apiVersion`, `kind` → each an @Error `package/invalid-manifest` finding
    addressed to file `package.yaml`, then dispatch to @check_options and
    @check_prerelease_versions); @check_unexpected_dirs; @run_hbs_checks (fresh
    @LintConfig::load a second time, fresh @HbsChecker::new); @run_rhai_checks (fresh
    @RhaiChecker::new with @package_dir, @config_dir, @script_dir.as_deref(), package,
    config); @prefix_files(@package_dir); @println! the filtered report; the junit lane;
    the @has_errors verdict.
  The first @LintConfig::load result (into `_config`) is dropped unused before the pipeline —
    dead state, the second load is the one that flows (Tasks `[?]`).
  # Structure rule
  @expected_dirs freezes the per-type expected sets: @VynilPackageType::System → `systems`,
    `crds`, `scripts`, `handlebars`; ::Service → `vitals`, `scalables`, `others`, `befores`,
    `posts`, `handlebars`, `scripts`, `crds`; ::Tenant → the Service set without `crds`.
  @check_unexpected_dirs inspects immediate children of @package_dir only: directories whose
    name does not start with `.`, is not in the expected set, and IS in the ten-name
    known list `systems`, `crds`, `vitals`, `scalables`, `others`, `befores`, `posts`,
    `pods`, `handlebars`, `scripts` → @Warn `package/unexpected-dir` per directory.
    Names outside that list (`tests/`, `notes/`, …) are never flagged; the known list hard
    includes `pods` which no type expects, so a `pods/` dir warns on every package
    (Tasks `[?]`).
  # Option-schema rules (@check_options, findings in @BTreeMap key order)
  Every @options value must be a JSON object; scalar/array/null → @Error
    `package/invalid-option-schema` (`got scalar value` wording even for arrays/null) and
    continue to the next option.
  Object → serde round-trip @serde_json::to_string then @serde_json::from_str::<@Schema>
    (the /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd openapiv3 re-export; this file does NOT call
    @VynilPackageSource::validate_options, it repeats the round-trip locally); rejection →
    @Error `invalid OpenAPI schema: {e}` and continue; the to_string failure path
    @unwrap_or_default-s to an empty string that then fails the from_str with an
    empty-input parse error (Tasks `[?]`).
  Surviving schema object must carry a type indicator key among `type`, `$ref`, `oneOf`,
    `anyOf`, `allOf`, else @Error `missing 'type' field` — and this branch does NOT continue:
    description and object-shape checks still run on it.
  Missing `description` key → @Info `package/option-missing-description`.
  `type` == `object` AND a `properties` key present → @Warn
    `package/object-properties-unsupported` pointing at the flat-default alternative.
  # Pre-release rule
  @is_prerelease is a lowercase-substring test: the version is @Warn-worthy iff its
    lowercased text contains `alpha`, `beta` or `rc` anywhere (Tasks `[?]` for the
    false-positive/false-negative edges).
  @check_prerelease_versions warns `package/prerelease-version` on @metadata.app_version when
    set-and-marked, and once per @images entry whose @Image.tag is set-and-marked, iterating
    the @BTreeMap in key order.
  # Line attribution (best-effort, @None tolerated, each call re-reads the manifest text)
  @find_line_with_key returns the first 1-based line whose left-trimmed text starts with
    `{key}:` (so an indented nested key can match) or @None.
  @find_image_tag_line runs a miniature indented-YAML scan: find the `images:` line, then the
    first entry line starting `{name}:` deeper than it, then the first deeper `tag:` line →
    its 1-based line, skipping blank and `#` lines, @None when the shape deviates
    (quoted keys, flow maps, multi-document).
  Option lines come from the delegated @find_option_line_numbers scan (pending).
  # Walk scope (all three scans, recursive)
  @run_hbs_checks does two full passes over the immediate subdirectories of @package_dir
    (every directory, hidden ones included): pass 1 @scan_hbs_files reads each `hbs`-extension
    file (extension match case-sensitive via @Path::extension) and feeds
    @HbsChecker::check_file with the @strip_prefix-relative path; pass 2
    @scan_rhai_files_for_values feeds every `rhai` source's text to
    @HbsChecker::scan_rhai_for_values/@scan_rhai_for_partials/@scan_rhai_for_images/
    @scan_rhai_for_resources (usage collection, emits nothing directly); then
    @HbsChecker::finalize findings (@Warn-level unused-helper/unused-partial/unused-option
    family, pending spec) are @extend-ed. Unreadable files are skipped silently; a file that
    won't strip-prefix is skipped.
  @run_rhai_checks walks the whole tree again for `rhai` files (@scan_rhai_files →
    @RhaiChecker::check_file, so every `.rhai` text is read twice across the two phases),
    then runs the inline lanes: @value_script under the virtual path
    `package.yaml#value_script`, then each @VynilPackageRequirement::Prefly in declaration
    order under `package.yaml#prefly({name})` ({name} is the requirement's own name), both
    through the identical @check_file path — the source comment asserts operator-context
    full-API with no import-resolution expected, honouring that is pending-side.
    @RhaiChecker::finalize findings (rhai/unused-script, rhai/unused-function, pending) are
    @extend-ed last.
  @prefix_files rewrites EVERY relative finding path (including the virtual
    `package.yaml#…` identities) onto @package_dir before printing, so files print absolute
    when `-p` is absolute.
  # Output, artifact and exit lanes
  stdout is exactly one @println! of @format_output: @Json → @to_json, @Text → @to_text
    (framing — `[LEVEL] rule file[:line]` blocks, the French `Résultat : N erreur(s),
    M warning` footer, the JSON findings/summary shape — owned by ./../linting/mod.rs,
    pending). The report prints on every non-early path and also on both early-return
    gates, always before any @Err.
  `--level` is display-only: it maps through @level_filter_to_lint_level into the collector's
    `>=` filter; it never changes which findings exist, which files prefix, whether junit is
    written, or the verdict.
  The junit lane runs only after the report println!, only when @junit_output_filename is
    @Some, writes @to_junit over the FULL unfiltered finding set via @std::fs::write
    (truncate-or-create, parents never created), and its @Err preempts the verdict @Err.
  Exit contract, frozen: @Err fires iff any finding has @LintLevel::Error —
    `@has_errors` tests equality with @Error only. Findings owned here that BLOCK exit:
    `package/missing-manifest`, `package/invalid-manifest` (both texts),
    `package/invalid-option-schema` (all three texts). Findings owned here that only WARN
    and keep @Ok → exit 0: `package/unexpected-dir`, `package/prerelease-version`,
    `package/object-properties-unsupported` (@Warn), `package/option-missing-description`
    (@Info). Delegated `hbs/…` and `rhai/…` findings feed the same verdict by their
    effective level; @LintConfig override/disable (pending) can demote even an Error-level
    rule to non-blocking or silence it entirely, so the blocking set is
    `.vynil-lint.yaml`-dependent through the checkers' @resolve_level call sites.
  # Posture and state
  Read-only over the package tree: this file writes exactly two things — stdout report via
    @println! and the optional junit file; no temp dirs, no mutations, nothing deleted.
  No cache and no cross-run state: manifest text is re-read per @find_line_with_key /
    @find_image_tag_line call, option lines are scanned once per @check_options run, and the
    two checkers keep only their own accumulator sets (helper/usage/import/function tracking,
    pending-owned) built eagerly at @new from directory listings.
  Panic posture frozen: product code here has zero @unwrap/@expect/@panic! and no indexing;
    every fallible std call is guarded (@if-@Ok on @read_dir/@read_to_string, @let-@Ok chains,
    @saturating_add/@saturating_sub in line math, @map_err on the junit write); the only
    reachable panic surface is the documented pending-side @to_junit.

Example:
  The seven rule codes owned by this file and all eleven distinct message templates, verbatim
    (interpolations in `{}`; `file` = `package.yaml` or the dir name, `line` = @None unless
    the locator resolves):
  - `package/missing-manifest` @Error — `package.yaml is missing`
  - `package/invalid-manifest` @Error — `Failed to parse package.yaml: {e}`
  - `package/invalid-manifest` @Error — `Missing required field: {field}` (field ∈ name,
      category, description, apiVersion, kind)
  - `package/unexpected-dir` @Warn — `Directory '{dir_name}' is not expected for {usage:?}
      packages` — {usage:?} is the @VynilPackageType @Debug rendering `Tenant`/`System`/
      `Service`
  - `package/prerelease-version` @Warn — `app_version '{app_version}' contains a pre-release
      marker (alpha/beta/rc)`
  - `package/prerelease-version` @Warn — `Image '{name}' tag '{tag}' contains a pre-release
      marker (alpha/beta/rc)`
  - `package/invalid-option-schema` @Error — `Option '{key}': must be an OpenAPI schema
      object, got scalar value`
  - `package/invalid-option-schema` @Error — `Option '{key}': invalid OpenAPI schema: {e}`
  - `package/invalid-option-schema` @Error — `Option '{key}': missing 'type' field in
      OpenAPI schema`
  - `package/option-missing-description` @Info — `Option '{key}': no description provided`
  - `package/object-properties-unsupported` @Warn — `Option '{key}': nested 'properties'
      sub-schema is not supported for type:object; use a flat 'default:' map at the option
      root instead`
  @Err-lane strings (all @Error::YamlError): `Missing package manifest`,
    `Invalid package manifest`, `Failed to write JUnit output: {e}`,
    `Linting failed with errors`.
  Delegated rule codes observed at these call sites only (levels/framing pending-owned, not
    enumerated): `hbs/syntax`, `hbs/unused-helper`, `hbs/unused-partial`, `hbs/unused-option`
    (./../linting/hbs_checker.rs) and `rhai/syntax`, `rhai/unresolved-import`,
    `rhai/unused-script`, `rhai/unused-function` plus the per-file AST rules
    (./../linting/rhai_checker.rs and its walker).

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover @expected_dirs + @check_unexpected_dirs: per-type expected sets, known-but-wrong
      dir warns, unknown dir silent, hidden dir silent, `pods/` warns on every type, the
      {usage:?} Debug rendering in the message.
  [ ] Cover @run end to end: missing-manifest gate (report prints before the @Err, no junit
      file on this path), parse-failure message interpolation, error-finding → @Err verdict,
      warn/Info-only → @Ok, and `--level` filtering the print but never the verdict.
  [ ] Cover @format_output both lanes and @level_filter_to_lint_level mapping (the pending
      collector carries the framing, but the selection branch is here).
  [ ] Cover the inline-script lane: `@value_script` present, @Prefly present, the exact
      post-prefix virtual files `…/package.yaml#value_script` and
      `…/package.yaml#prefly({name})`, and multiple-prefly ordering.
  [ ] Cover the recursive walkers: nested `.hbs`/`.rhai` discovery, hidden-directory
      inclusion, uppercase-extension files skipped, unreadable file silently skipped,
      unreadable directory truncating the walk silently.
  [ ] Cover @find_line_with_key and @find_image_tag_line attribution: found, indented
      false-match, comment/blank skip, missing key → @None line on the finding.
  [ ] Cover @is_prerelease boundaries: the three markers cased-insensitively (partly covered
      via @app_version tests), plus a stable version containing an `rc`/`beta` letter run
      that the substring rule flags.
  [ ] Cover the `--junit-output-filename` lane: file written after the stdout report, writes
      the unfiltered set, write failure @Err preempts the verdict @Err.
  [?] @LintConfig::load is called twice in @run (L214 result bound to `_config` and dropped;
      L258 load feeds the checkers). Decide whether the first load is vestigial and remove it.
  [?] The scan walkers swallow every @read_dir/@read_to_string failure behind `if let @Ok`/
      `let @Ok` guards and always return @Ok(@()), so the `@Result` returns and `?` lanes of
      @run_hbs_checks/@run_rhai_checks are dead and their `# Errors` doc comments ("returns
      … when directory walks fail at OS level") are wrong: an unreadable subtree is linters-
      blind silently. Decide whether walk failures should surface (as findings or @Err).
  [?] Four @Err lanes all reuse @common::Error::YamlError though only the parse lane is YAML:
      missing manifest drops the filesystem detail entirely, "Linting failed with errors" is
      a generic non-YAML payload, and a @std::io::Error junit write failure is re-wrapped as
      YamlError text. Decide per-variant identity (bootstrap.project stable-error-identity
      rule leans on message uniqueness only).
  [?] @is_prerelease matches `alpha`/`beta`/`rc` as substrings anywhere in the lowercased
      text — a tag such as `2.1-orce-1` or a version word containing `rc`/`beta` warns, while
      other pre-release idioms (`preview`, `snapshot`, `dev`, `latest`) pass; no semver
      pre-release structure is consulted (contrast /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd @Semver).
      Decide whether to parse properly.
  [?] `"pods"` sits in the known-directory list of @check_unexpected_dirs but no
      @expected_dirs arm expects it, so any `pods/` directory warns under every package type.
      Decide whether `pods` is a future type directory or a stale list entry.
  [?] `-c`/`@config_dir` is help-labelled `Configuration directory`, yet @LintConfig reads
      `.vynil-lint.yaml` only from @package_dir — config_dir only extends the Rhai import
      resolver. Decide whether the lint config should also resolve from it or the help text
      should change.
  [?] Docs drift, both against this frozen behaviour: /docs/cli.md's exit table claims
      `2: lint with warnings only` while warn-only lint is @Ok → exit 0, and
      /docs/tooling/lint.md advertises `--format junit` while the flag accepts only
      `text`/`json`. Fix docs (agent.sdd pins cli.md stable — docs owner, not this file).
  [?] @check_options labels every non-object value as `got scalar value` even for JSON arrays
      and @null, and its @serde_json::to_string @unwrap_or_default path turns a serialization
      failure into a misleading `invalid OpenAPI schema` parse error on empty input. Decide
      faithful wording/error handling.
  [?] @check_options_non_object_with_properties_key_no_extra_warn (the #[cfg(test)] lane) is
      mislabelled: its fixture has no `properties` key at all, so the branch its name claims
      (non-object carrying `properties`) stays untested. Rename or fix the fixture.
  [?] @OutputFormat is duplicated between this file and ./test.rs (identical text/json
      ValueEnums); the shared-or-duplicate decision already sits `[?]` in ./test.sdd — keep
      one home for it.

Done when:
  Each Scenario above carries mapped passing tests and every Tasks coverage hole closes, the
    `[?]` decisions are recorded, and `cargo test -p agent`, clippy and `cargo +nightly
    fmt --check` stay green.

Scenario: missing manifest short-circuits before any checker
  Given `-p /pkg` with no `package.yaml` (also a nonexistent `/pkg`)
  When @run runs
  Then exactly one report prints — the `package/missing-manifest` Error block plus the
    collector tally — showing the prefixed file path
  And @Err @Error::YamlError("Missing package manifest") returns; ./mod.sdd logs the exit-1
    line; the `hbs`/`rhai`/option/prerelease lanes never execute and no junit file is written
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: unparsable manifest reports the parse detail then fails
  Given a `package.yaml` holding `metadata: "nope"` (or unreadable bytes)
  When @run runs
  Then the `package/invalid-manifest` Error finding interpolates the @serde_yaml message as
    `Failed to parse package.yaml: {e}` and prints before the @Err
    @Error::YamlError("Invalid package manifest")
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Errors block, warnings only pass — the exit-1 contract
  Given a run whose findings mix levels (e.g. one `package/invalid-option-schema` @Error plus
    a `package/prerelease-version` @Warn) versus warn-only versus clean
  When @run runs
  Then the mixed and warn-only runs print the full report while only the mixed run returns
    @Err("Linting failed with errors"); warn-only and clean return @Ok(@()) and exit 0
  And `--level error` hides the @Warn from the print but neither adds nor removes
    blocking findings, and `--level all` (default) additionally shows @Info items like
    `package/option-missing-description` without changing anything else
  Mapped tests cover only the level-independent helper verdicts (@has_errors via
    @check_options/@check_manifest_fields tests); the exit contract itself has none.

Scenario: unexpected known directory warns per type
  Given `type: system` with sibling directories `vitals/` (Service/Tenant-only), `notes/`
    (unknown) and `.git/` (hidden)
  When @run runs
  Then exactly one `package/unexpected-dir` @Warn prints for `vitals` with the Debug-rendered
    `not expected for System packages` text; `notes` and `.git` produce nothing
  And a `pods/` directory would warn under every type (frozen oddity, Tasks `[?]`)
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: inline scripts report under virtual manifest paths
  Given a package with `value_script:` set and two @Prefly requirements named `auth` and `net`
  When @run_rhai_checks runs
  Then @RhaiChecker::check_file runs first on `package.yaml#value_script`, then on
    `package.yaml#prefly(auth)` and `package.yaml#prefly(net)` in requirement order, and any
    findings come back filed under those virtual files after @prefix_files
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: option schema findings cascade on one key
  Given option `solver` = `{"type": "object", "properties": {…}}` (valid indicator, no
    description, nested properties)
  When @check_options runs
  Then the type-indicator pass does not short-circuit the later rules: `@Info` `no description
    provided` and `@Warn` `nested 'properties' sub-schema is not supported …` both fire on the
    same key at the option's scanned line
  But Given `solver2` = `{"type": "object", "default": {"k": "v"}, "description": "…"}` —
    clean, no warn, the flat-default shape
  And Given a scalar option `n = 42` → the `got scalar value` @Error and none of the
    description/properties checks
  Mapped tests @check_options_object_with_nested_properties_warns,
    @check_options_object_with_flat_default_passes, @check_options_scalar_reports_key_name,
    @check_options_missing_description_is_info pin the pieces; the simultaneous
    Info+Warn cascade on one key is not asserted.

Scenario: pre-release markers warn with best-effort lines
  Given `app_version: 1.0.0-ALPHA.1` and `images.app.tag: v1-rc2` with the tag lines present
    in the manifest text
  When @check_prerelease_versions runs
  Then both `package/prerelease-version` @Warns print, line-located via @find_line_with_key /
    @find_image_tag_line (the uppercase `ALPHA` matches the lowercase substring rule)
  But Given a manifest where the tag line is unrecognizable to the mini-YAML scan — the finding
    still prints with @None line
  Mapped tests @check_prerelease_versions_* pin the warn/no-warn matrix on in-memory models;
    line attribution itself has none.
